# Architecture

Before changing structure or adding modules, read:

- `CONTEXT.md` — domain vocabulary (use these terms; avoid listed synonyms)
- `docs/adr/0001-module-boundaries.md` — backend module DAG
- `docs/adr/0002-frontend-vertical-slices.md` — frontend feature slices

## Quick map

| Concern | Lives in |
|---|---|
| Domain words | `CONTEXT.md` |
| Backend feature | `apps/backend/src/<feature>/` deep module |
| Frontend feature UI | `apps/frontend/src/features/<name>/` |
| Thin routes | `apps/frontend/src/routes/` compose only |
| Shared FE infra/UI | `apps/frontend/src/shared/` |
| Hard decisions | `docs/adr/` |

## Non-negotiables

1. **Import DAG, no cycles** — dependencies point down (routers → cores → adapters → infra). Features do not import other features’ implementations.
2. **Deep modules** — small `createX(deps)` interface; composition only in `index.ts`.
3. **Thin edges** — tRPC routers and FE routes carry no business UI/logic.
4. **Vocabulary** — say Title, Catalog, WatchTask, Transfer, Topic as in `CONTEXT.md`.

When a new term or seam is decided, update `CONTEXT.md` / add an ADR — don’t leave it only in chat.
